                        


Item #: SCP-5156

Object Class: Euclid

Special Containment Procedures: SCP-5156-01 is to be contained in an airtight soundproofed cell, measuring 10m x 10m x 10m . The interior and exterior is to be lined with 1 inch thick tungsten sheets, separated by 16 inches concrete. The cell is only accessible by a series of three tungsten doors, each 6 inches thick. The ceiling of the cell is to be equipped with 4, 30,000 watt, UV lights, one in each corner of the cell. Only personnel with level 2 clearance are allowed to enter SCP-5156-01’s containment cell.

SCP-5156-02 is to be kept in a 4 meter locked room, one level 3 security officer is to be stationed outside the room at all times. Only personnel with level 3 clearance are to enter the room, anyone attempting to damage or steal SCP-5156-02 is to be terminated immediately.

Description: SCP-5156-01 is a sexless hairless bipedal humanoid entity measuring 4 meters tall while standing erect. It has very little body mass and no pigment in it’s skin, similar to SCP-096. The arms and legs of SCP-5156-01 are covered in deep cuts and scratches, exposing the entity’s muscular system. The entity has no visible hands or fingers, but it is suspected to have perfectly invisible claws. SCP-5156-01’s feet are replaced by stumps, after close investigation it has been concluded the entity once had feet but were since amputated by an unknown source. On the back of the entity’s neck there is a symbol burned into its flesh, which has been identified as the aztec miquiztli, which translates to death; it is unknown how or why SCP-5156-01 received this mark. The creature's face is relatively human in appearance, it’s eyes sink 2 inches into the skull of SCP-5156-01. The jaw of the entity can open twice the normal amount of a human. SCP-5156-01 has 2 rows of human teeth.

SCP-5156-02 is a large glass helmet measuring 3 meters in diameter.

Addendum:

Both SCP-5156-01 and 02 were first discovered in __ Mexico on July 4th, 2019 after a series of unknown disappearances caught the attention of Maria Lopez, a level 3 Scientist for the foundation who was on vacation at the time. The following is a transcript of the audio logs taken during the investigation

4:30 am

Dr. Lopez: July 4th 2019. This is Dr. Maria Lopez, along with a native I will be investigating a possible anomaly located in __ Mexico.

5:27 am

Dr. Lopez: We have been walking for around an hour, in front of me is a strange pile of red ooze, I assume it is blood of some kind. In the distance I can see more of the piles.

5:46 am

Dr. Lopez: I have started seeing things running through the forest, they are much too fast for me to fully see.

Native whistles*


Dr. Lopez: My associate has given me ear protection, may I ask why are these necessary?

Native: No good English, protect from screams.

Dr. Lopez: Screams? What screams?

screeching from behind *
A loud thump followed by what sounds to be a struggle between Dr. Lopez and an unknown entity *


*Gunshot*

*Dr.Lopez breathing heavily*

Dr. Lopez: Thank you Amigo. I was just attacked by some kind of primate. Hold on, it may be the heat getting to me but at first glance the creature appears to be a Homo Habilis. Interesting.

6:19 am

*Loud screams muffle Dr. Lopez’s words*

Audio Logs end

Dr. Lopez later describes a strange Aztec temple, inside she found SCP-5156-01 chained to a wall, SCP-5156-02 sat on a pedestal in the center of the room.

SCP-5156-01 displays two anomalous qualities. At all times the entity emits a deafening scream, those unfortunate enough to hear it begin an anomalous transformation, which will be referred to as SCP-5156-03. SCP-5156-03 has been proven to not affect any other species. Exposure to the scream causes a human to rapidly devolve, this devolution stops at Homo Habilis. After 3 days any instance of SCP-5156-03 will explode due to unknown means, all attempts to prevent this outcome have failed. The only known way to silence SCP-5156-01’s scream is to place SCP-5156-02 on its head. Although SCP-5156-01 has no visible claws it has been seen making scratching motion over its skin and at the door, After examination it appears SCP-5156-01 is equipped with perfectly transparent claws capable of cutting through steel.

Three tests have been performed using SCP-5156-02. In each test SCP-5156-01 was subdued and locked to a large tungsten chair, SCP-5156-02 placed over it’s head. The tests prove that the entity is sentient, when shown various images the entity displayed several emotions, these include smiling, crying, and scowling. When shown a picture of the mark on its neck it displayed great amounts of shame, hanging its head and weeping. Dr. Lopez Requested a sketch of SCP-096 to be shown to SCP-5156-01, she was, “Curious if it knew who SCP-096 was, given the two’s similar appearance.”. Upon seeing the sketch SCP-5156-01 displayed extreme distress. The Entity shook violently and screamed louder than ever previously recorded, Noise sensors recorded over 200 decibels. The screams caused a large crack in SCP-5156-02. SCP- 5156-01 shook it’s head violently, flinging SCP-5156-02 off of its head. All personnel present died later that week due to cases of SCP-5156-03. After the incident no further tests have been performed.

                    

                                    





            
    

                    



                    
                        
                            
